raising babies dragon into adult is a long and tedious process. Maybe
letting them play in the (ex) pudding farm good be a good way to raise
them fast... Killing your pet is not a nice idea after that.

> B) Polymorph my pet?  I don't have a good pet and this could be really
> useful.  Only problem is it's kind of risky and I might totally use up
> the wand of polymorph without getting anything good.

Try with several pets in a line, it's better. And you may end up with
rather good pets after emptying a wand. All you have to do is know when to
stop. "le mieux est l'ennemi du bien".

> C) Polymorph items?  I'm in a pudding farm right now so naturally there
> are a lot of items laying about.  Should I try polypiling and hope for
> a magic marker or other useful goods?

Most dropped items are probably useless, so that could be a good idea
(typically to turn useless scrolls into usefull one, or already known
spellbooks into new one).

Another nice thing to try is to build over-enchanting weapon :
Gather arrows (either lying in the dungeon or pudding-farmed).
Enchant them to +7.
Make a few separate stacks.
Try to enchant each stack separately.
rinse, repeat.
You should end up with some +8, +9 or even +10 arrows (and a lot will
dissapear in the process).
Polypile them into +10 usefull weapon.

Similar trick can probably be done with elven armor to get +7 usual armor.

